<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 7 July, from 1456 to 2005.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1456</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc is cleared of heresy 25 years after her death</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A retrial authorised by Pope Callixtus III quashed Joan of Arc's 1431 conviction and declared her innocent. She was canonised as a saint in 1920.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1777</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American rearguard fights the British at Hubbardton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Retreating from Fort Ticonderoga, an American rearguard fought pursuing British and German troops at Hubbardton, Vermont. Though defeated, they slowed Burgoyne's advance towards eventual surrender at Saratoga.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1898</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President McKinley signs the resolution annexing Hawaii</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">McKinley signed the Newlands Resolution, annexing the Republic of Hawaii five years after American businessmen had overthrown Queen Liliuokalani. Hawaii became a US territory and, in 1959, the 50th state.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1937</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marco Polo Bridge Incident sparks war between China and Japan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A night-time clash between Japanese and Chinese troops at the Marco Polo Bridge near Beijing escalated into full-scale war. The Second Sino-Japanese War merged into the Second World War and cost millions of Chinese lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1985</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Boris Becker, 17, becomes Wimbledon's youngest men's champion</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Unseeded West German Boris Becker beat Kevin Curren in four sets to win Wimbledon at 17. He remains the youngest men's singles champion in the tournament's history.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">2005</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Suicide bombers kill 52 on London's transport network</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four bombers struck three Underground trains and a bus during the morning rush hour, killing 52 people. It was Britain's deadliest terrorist attack since Lockerbie, a day after London won the 2012 Olympics.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li></ol>
